  "why": "the chip's two biggest clock loads here are models: vpu_64x32_3r2w_vpurf and vpu_tensorc_rf_buffer_array are compiled macros with one clock pin each, not 2,243 + 562 latches behind per-entry gates, and vpu_bypass's clock is held off for the whole TensorFMA (vpu_ctrl.v ll.1244, 1334, 1403, 1463, 1538 -> vpu_lane.v l.218, l.245). The three real latch files (TENA, TENB x2, TMP) are rf_latch_1r_1w in the chip too and stay. Clock-tree energy tracks the pin load the tree drives, so the share of the pin load that survives bounds it below; the two macros' own clock pins are a few fF and are not added back"
 },
